      {
        "id": "s1_parts",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "The four parts",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Parts and kidneys",
        "why": "Naming the four parts first gives the answer its shape, because everything after it is a description of one of them.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Naming the skin or lungs. The question asks for the excretory system proper.",
          "Leaving out the hilum. It is the notch the vessels enter by."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Kidneys, ureters, bladder, urethra — top to bottom.",
        "margin_note": "Four parts, then the kidney from the outside.",
        "lines": [
          "The human excretory system has 4 parts:",
          "1. A pair of kidneys",
          "2. A pair of ureters",
          "3. Urinary bladder",
          "4. Urethra",
          {
            "text": "1. Kidneys",
            "style": "heading"
          },
          "They are reddish brown, bean shaped,",
          "retroperitoneal organs.",
          "They lie on either side of the vertebral",
          "column at the level of the anterior lumbar",
          "vertebrae.",
          "The outer surface is convex and the inner",
          "surface concave with a deep notch, the",
          "hilum."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s2_kidney_internal",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "Inside the kidney",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Cortex and medulla",
        "why": "The two regions are not just layers: the filtering parts of the nephron sit in the cortex and the concentrating parts in the medulla.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Swapping the regions. The cortex is outer, the medulla inner.",
          "Leaving out the columns of Bertini. They are a marked name."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Cortex outside, medulla inside, pyramids in the medulla.",
        "margin_note": "Four points cover this mark.",
        "lines": [
          "Internally the kidney has two regions, the",
          "outer cortex and the inner medulla.",
          "The cortex holds the malpighian capsules",
          "and the proximal and distal convoluted",
          "tubules of the nephrons.",
          "The medulla is divided into cone shaped",
          "masses called renal pyramids.",
          "Renal columns, the columns of Bertini,",
          "separate the pyramids. They are",
          "projections of cortex into the medulla."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "s3_ureter_bladder",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "Ureters, bladder, urethra",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "The other three parts",
        "why": "Once urine is made it only has to be carried, stored and released, which is what these three parts do in turn.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Confusing ureter and urethra. Ureters carry urine to the bladder; the urethra carries it out.",
          "Leaving out the two sphincters of the urethra."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Ureter goes to the bladder, urethra goes to the outside.",
        "margin_note": "One or two lines each. Do not spend long here.",
        "lines": [
          {
            "text": "2. Ureters",
            "style": "heading"
          },
          "Two slender whitish tubes emerge from the",
          "pelvis of the kidneys, run downwards and",
          "open into the urinary bladder.",
          {
            "text": "3. Urinary bladder",
            "style": "heading"
          },
          "It is a median storage sac in the lower",
          "abdominal cavity.",
          {
            "text": "4. Urethra",
            "style": "heading"
          },
          "The neck of the bladder leads into the",
          "urethra, which has an internal and an",
          "external urethral sphincter."
        ]
      },
